Generate T120 I/O from EasyEDA project information Example T120 FPGA
1. Open EasyEDA PCB view.
1.1 Export project by do: File -> Files source -> Donwload
1.2 Extract Inverted_MAML_IMC.epro2 zip file

unzip Inverted_MAML_IMC.epro2 -d Inverted_MAML_IMC

2. Create a minimum template I/O Interface description from Efinix GUI tool generated a 
T120_MALM.peri.xml
cope and rename to 
T120_MALM_template.peri.xml

3. Collect Pin map data from Efinix pin map excel data 
create a 
T120_pin_map.xlsx 

4. Run script:

python3 t120_easyeda_mapper.py \
  --source Inverted_MAML_IMC/Inverted_MAML_IMC.epru \
  --pinout T120_pin_map.xlsx \
  --json olle_test1_t120_connection.json \
  --report olle_Test1_connection_report.txt \
  --xml-template T120_MALM_template.peri.xml \
  --xml-output T120_MALM.generated.peri.xml

5. Put back the 
T120_MALM.generated.peri.xml
to Efinix project path and overwrite the orginal interface specification ther
T120_MALM.peri.xml